<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI8-IMPORTANT-02-NEWTYPES>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI8-IMPORTANT-02-NEWTYPES" ;
  triage:title "Contract's typed newtypes CertificateFingerprint/PrivateKeyRef downgraded to raw String" ;
  triage:resolution "FIXED in integrate/phase-AI @ 98e6fc38 (PR #603, commit 2196ffb3). Peer config newtypes (HostName, HttpsInterface, CertificateFingerprint, TrustedPeer, LocalCertificate, PrivateKeyRef) are properly defined and serialize/deserialize correctly in peer.rs. Type safety enforced across trust boundaries." ;
  triage:description "AI8-QA-1 (ruthless-boundary RBQA-F003, rust-best-practices RBP-F001 — 2 independent confirmations). The approved sprint contract declares CertificateFingerprint/PrivateKeyRef newtypes; the shipped HttpsInterface/LocalCertificate/TrustedPeer (crates/atm-storage/src/contract.rs:472-492) use plain String with the same non-blank check re-implemented independently in 4+ places (storage, runtime composition, CLI). This loses the compile-time guarantee that a fingerprint can't be passed where a key-ref is expected — exactly the two fields the sprint calls 'security-sensitive.' Using raw String prevents type-system enforcement of the semantic difference between these security-critical values." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "important" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI8-IMPORTANT-02-NEWTYPES/pAI-8/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-8/d9991a90> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-8/d9991a90> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s8-crosshost-control-plane" ;
  triage:highestFixedBranch "integrate/phase-AI" ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-20T19:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:notes "Fix: either (1) adopt CertificateFingerprint/PrivateKeyRef newtypes per the documented contract and thread them through HttpsInterface/LocalCertificate/TrustedPeer, or (2) record an explicit deviation note in the requirements explaining why the newtypes were abandoned. Newtypes are strongly preferred for security-sensitive values." .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI8-IMPORTANT-02-NEWTYPES/pAI-8/1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
